<title>ESTONIA: COMPENSATION FUND FEB PROFIT WAS 11.8 MLN EEK.</title>
<headline>COMPENSATION FUND FEB PROFIT WAS 11.8 MLN EEK.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>- The Compensation Fund said on Wednesday that its February profit was 11.8 million kroons, down compared to January's 13.6 million kroons.</p>
<p>The Fund's balance sheet volume was up to 1.2 billion kroons, a growth by 3.8 percent compared to January's results, it said in statement.</p>
<p>Invesments increased the Fund's assets by 32.1 percent or 33.9 million kroons in February to 139.5 million kroons, the Compensation Fund added.</p>
<p>The Compensation Fund is a state fund set up to make compensation to people relating to privatisation claims.</p>
<p>-- David Mardiste, Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
